<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konkan coast</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Konkan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Konkan coast is the strip of land along the western coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ghats">Western Ghats</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a>. It was strategically important to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a>, which built coastal forts and a navy there. Maratha naval commanders operating from the Konkan contested control of the coast with European powers and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siddis">Siddis</a> of Janjira.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/konkan-coast.jpg" alt="Konkan coast" width="320" height="158" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saishg at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dabhol_Beach.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
